  "title": "Linda K Probable NDE 125",
  "date": "Christmas of 1992",
  "content": "I was post-surgery for bowel obstruction and had developed pneumonia. I was not responding to the antibiotics and had an IV in each arm and one of those gastric tubes down my nose. I was losing strength every day, and eventually the morphine would not touch the pain. I began to pray that I would die. After a very long intense time, I was released from my body, began to float upwards, and became aware of a light, not a tunnel but a light. As I got closer to the light, I could see an angel and she held her arms out to me but I never made it into her arms. I said to her, 'I am here,' and she said, 'You must go back.' I asked, 'But why?' She said, 'You must think of the children.' I had been so miserable that I had forgotten all about my children! I returned immediately to my body, and by the way, to immediately heal! I was out of the hospital in forty-eight hours! It took me two years to get over the surgery, but I'll never get over the experience",
